data.value:
CUSTOS for Linux {0}
Usage: custos status the service, the tasks and the connection to the site custos run <task> start a task now (its name or id); custos run --all starts every task custos stop [<task>] stop the run in progress (or the run of that task) custos log [-f] [-n N] the last lines of the journal; -f keeps showing new ones custos snapshots whether the volumes of the tasks can have snapshots, and what to do if not custos connect '<line>' connect to the monitoring site (the connection line from the site) custos disconnect disconnect from the site custos version the version
Tasks are created and changed on the monitoring site. Service log: /var/log/custos.
